 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The person who receives",
     "texto": [
      "The pronouns **me, te, le, nos, os, les** say **who receives** something or who benefits. They go **before the verb**.\n\n- **Le** doy un regalo (to Ana).\n- ¿**Me** prestas tu libro?\n- **Les** escribo (to my parents).\n\n**Le** works for he, she and usted. **Os** goes with vosotros, mainly in Spain; with ustedes you say **les**.\n\nThe person is often repeated: **Le** doy un regalo **a Ana**. Compare: **la** veo (I look at her) and **le** escribo (I write to her)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "The six pronouns",
     "texto": [
      "Each person has its pronoun:\n\n- **yo** → **me**: ¿Me prestas tu libro?\n- **tú** → **te**: Te presto veinte euros.\n- **él, ella, usted** → **le**: Le doy un regalo.\n- **nosotros** → **nos**: Ana nos presta sus libros.\n- **vosotros** → **os**: Os digo la verdad.\n- **ellos, ellas, ustedes** → **les**: Les escribo hoy.\n\nTypical verbs: **dar, decir, prestar, escribir, regalar, enviar, pedir, traer**."
     ],
